ATLAS: upstream llama.cpp bug fix (applied with `git apply`, which skips this text).

graph_reserve() rounds n_tokens up to a multiple of n_seqs but kept
n_outputs as requested. A context with --embeddings --pooling mean
reserves with n_outputs == n_tokens, so with --parallel N where N does
not divide the ubatch size (ATLAS: 6 slots, -ub 2048) mean pooling
multiplied an n_outputs-row matrix by an n_tokens-wide mask and
llama-server aborted at startup:
  GGML_ASSERT(ggml_can_mul_mat(a, b)) failed  (llm_graph_context::build_pooling)
Keep "every token is an output" true after the rounding.

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
index 9ee64b5..9aad057 100644
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -2624,7 +2624,13 @@ ggml_cgraph * llama_context::graph_reserve(
     GGML_ASSERT(n_outputs >= 1);
 
     if (n_tokens % n_seqs != 0) {
+        const uint32_t n_tokens_req = n_tokens;
         n_tokens = ((n_tokens + (n_seqs - 1)) / n_seqs) * n_seqs; // round to next multiple of n_seqs
+        // ATLAS: a graph that outputs every token (pooled embeddings) must keep doing so,
+        // otherwise mean pooling multiplies n_outputs rows by an n_tokens-wide mask and aborts
+        if (n_outputs == n_tokens_req) {
+            n_outputs = n_tokens;
+        }
         LLAMA_LOG_DEBUG("%s: making n_tokens a multiple of n_seqs - n_tokens = %u, n_seqs = %u, n_outputs = %u\n", __func__, n_tokens, n_seqs, n_outputs);
     }
 
